    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43779" root="&#xA;                        ميل&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَالَ</span></b> 
                         [<i>He</i>, or <i>it, inclined, leant, bent, propended, tended, declined, deviated,</i> or <i>deflected.</i>]
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَالَ مَعَهُ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَايَلَهُ</span></b> 
                        <i>He conformed with,</i> and
<i>assisted,</i> or <i>aided, him.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَالَ إِلَيْهِ</span>
                        <i>He
loved him.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <i>He wronged him.</i>
(TA.) <i>He was,</i> or <i>became, inimical to him.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَالَتِ الدَّابَّةُ مِنْ رِجْلِهَا</span> (K, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غمز</span>,) <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَلَعَتْ</span>
[It <i>limped</i>]. (TA.)

